wn":9.2,"_gate_insider_buying":0.5,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":50.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Alexandria Real Estate Equities, Inc., is a mission-driven life science REIT. The firm is pioneered the life science real estate niche. The firm is the preeminent and longest-tenured owner, operator and developer of collaborative Megacampus ecosystems in AAA life science and advanced technology innovation cluster locations, including Greater Boston, the San Francisco Bay Area, San Diego, Seattle, Maryland, Research Triangle and New York City. Alexandria Real Estate Equities, Inc. was established on 5th January 1994 and was incorporated in Maryland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Peter M. Moglia | CEO & Chief Investment Officer | Age 58 | Compensation: $2.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 514 people. Revenue per employee of $5.9M ranks in the above the sector median among Real Estate peers, improving at 13%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $80K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Alexandria Real Estate Equities is a mid-cap real estate business with a $7.8B market cap on $3.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +5% over the past three years and +14% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Accruals are elevated at -8.3% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 8.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss.","Management returns a meaningful 14.3% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 689% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.8% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Real Estate sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Alexandria Real Estate Equities (ARE) \u2013 Investment Analysts\u2019 Weekly Ratings Changes","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/04/alexandria-real-estate-equities-are-investment-analysts-weekly-ratings-changes.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793813216.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.052,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Alexandria Real Estate Equities (ARE) Could Be 16% Undervalued As Impairments Deepen Losses",